From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:12:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: keep the first link when a later AP MLD link fails

A later link of an AP MLD takes the driver instance of the first link
(hapd->drv_priv = h_hapd->drv_priv) in hostapd_driver_init() and joins
the MLD only after hostapd_drv_link_add() succeeds. When that call, or
the check for driver MLO support, fails, the link returns -1 with the
borrowed pointer still set.

The caller's cleanup, hostapd_deinit_driver(), then treats the instance
as its own: hostapd_cleanup_driver() removes the link with this BSS's
link ID from the shared instance, which is the link of another BSS when
the link IDs collide, or deinits the instance when it looks unshared.
The first link keeps a pointer to a torn down or freed instance, and the
next link that is set up calls get_capa() on it and crashes hostapd.

Seen with an AP MLD whose links span two wiphys: the link on the second
wiphy was assigned link ID 0, hostapd_drv_link_add() refused it, and the
cleanup removed link 0 of the first wiphy.

A link that never joined the MLD now drops the borrowed instance before
it returns, so the cleanup leaves the first link alone.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@ setup_mld:
 		if (!(iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MLO)) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
 				   "MLD: Not supported by the driver");
-			return -1;
+			goto fail_mld;
 		}
 
 		/* Initialize the BSS parameter change to 1 */
@@ -388,13 +388,23 @@ setup_mld:
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
 				   "MLD: Failed to add link %d in MLD %s",
 				   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
-			return -1;
+			goto fail_mld;
 		}
 		hostapd_mld_add_link(hapd);
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	return 0;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+fail_mld:
+	/* A later link only borrowed the driver instance of the first link */
+	if (h_hapd) {
+		hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+		hapd->interface_added = 0;
+	}
+	return -1;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 }
 
 
